{
  "name": "OGC Building Blocks - Generic Provenance",
  "abstract": "Generic provenance profile aggregating W3C PROV, Wf4Ever and EOAP building blocks",
  "description": "These OGC Building Blocks provide a generic **provenance profile** for the\nOSPD / EOAP context, built on top of the canonical\n[W3C PROV](https://www.w3.org/TR/prov-overview/) data model (PROV-DM / PROV-O).\n\nRather than redefining PROV, this register **builds on** the W3C PROV JSON\nschema building block [`ogc.ogc-utils.prov`](https://ogcincubator.github.io/bblock-prov-schema/)\nand **aggregates** it with two complementary registers so they can be\ncross-referenced from a single place:\n\n- **[bblock-prov-schema](https://github.com/ogcincubator/bblock-prov-schema)**\n  (`ogc.ogc-utils.prov*`) \u2014 the canonical W3C PROV-O Entity / Activity / Agent\n  schemas that this register profiles.\n- **[bblocks-wf4ever](https://github.com/ogcincubator/bblocks-wf4ever)**\n  (`ogc.bbr.wf4ever.*`) \u2014 workflow-level provenance (wfdesc / wfprov / ro),\n  e.g. `wfprov:WorkflowRun`, for retrospective execution provenance.\n- **[bblocks-eoap-cct](https://github.com/ogcincubator/bblocks-eoap-cct)**\n  (`eoap.cct.*`) \u2014 EOAP CWL custom types (STAC, GeoJSON, bbox) used to type the\n  entities whose provenance is described.\n\nThe register defines the three core PROV starting-point classes as thin\nprofiles of the prov-schema sub-schemas, plus a provenance bundle:\n\n- **Entity** \u2014 profile of `ogc.ogc-utils.prov-entity`.\n- **Activity** \u2014 profile of `ogc.ogc-utils.prov-activity`.\n- **Agent** \u2014 profile of `ogc.ogc-utils.prov-agent`.\n- **Provenance (bundle)** \u2014 built on the `ogc.ogc-utils.prov` provenance chain.\n",
